<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nongsang jiyao</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1273</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Essentials of Agriculture and Sericulture</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Nongsang jiyao ('Essentials of Agriculture and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sericulture">Sericulture</a>') is a Chinese agricultural handbook compiled by the Yuan government's Office for the Stimulation of Agriculture and issued in 1273. Drawing on earlier treatises, it covered grain farming, silkworm raising, mulberry and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> cultivation, and was distributed to officials to help restore farming in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> after decades of war.</p></div>
